+   fresh attributes. Every other entry is advertised with the attributes from the
+   readdir() reply, which is what makes readdirplus pay off: whole-tree metadata walks
+   (git status, git diff --stat, rsync) stop costing one round trip per file.
+
+   Note that sshfs.conntab is only populated when more than one SFTP connection is in
+   use. With a single connection everything (including readdir) is serialized over the
+   same SFTP channel, so a readdir() issued after a write() is executed after it on the
+   server and its attributes cannot be stale - no suppression is needed there.
