+-o readdirplus=BOOL
+   Hand the file attributes that come with the directory listing to the
+   kernel, so that a metadata walk over a tree (``git status``,
+   ``git diff --stat``, ``rsync``) costs one round trip per *directory*
+   instead of one per file. The attributes are part of the SFTP
+   readdir reply anyway, so this costs nothing extra.
+
+   Entries that have a pending write are always excluded and fall back
+   to a normal *getattr()*, because a pending write can change a file's
+   length and the attributes from the listing would be stale. Possible
+   values: ``yes`` (default), ``no``, ``auto``.
+
